{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Slipstream and In My Soul feel like natural follow-ups to Memphis and Old Sock because blues guitar, soulful singing, and roots-oriented songs are what appeal to me right now.",
    "The acoustic blues and stripped-down performances also connect with my interests, even when I would save those albums for a later visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wallflower and Adele's 21 lean toward vocal pop, which does not satisfy my current interest in guitar-led blues.",
    "The Goat Rodeo Sessions and Coming from Reality offer instrumental strings or folk-oriented material, but those qualities alone do not give me the blues sound I want today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat a broad interest in established performers as enough reason for me to want their music, even when the sound differs from what I want now.",
    "Acoustic instruments and roots connections seem to count too heavily as signs of a match; I do not find every folk, string, or stripped-down recording equally appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Memphis, Old Sock, and People, Hell & Angels points toward blues feeling and expressive guitar playing, which matter more to me today than a broad connection to older music.",
    "An album can fit my taste without making me want to act now: I would choose Slipstream and In My Soul, while leaving relevant live sets and unfamiliar albums for another visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in blues and roots music, but stretch it too broadly into pop, folk, and instrumental recordings."
}"}
